# Nancy & Marc's Wedding Invitation

A single-page wedding invitation site with RSVP tracking, table-assignment QR codes, and calendar reminders — built for our wedding on **October 24, 2026** in Cairo.

## What's inside

- **Invitation** — ceremony & reception details, Mark 10:9, countdown timer
- **RSVP** — guests confirm attendance and whether they're bringing a +1
- **Table QR codes** — once we assign a guest's table, a QR code with their table number appears automatically when they revisit the site
- **Add to Calendar** — one tap adds the ceremony/reception to a guest's phone calendar, so they get a native reminder the day before
- **Admin panel** — tap the small monogram in the footer 5 times and enter the passcode to view all RSVPs and assign table numbers

## Tech

- Single static file: `index.html` (HTML/CSS/vanilla JS, no build step)
- [Firebase Firestore](https://firebase.google.com/) (free Spark plan) for storing RSVPs
- [QRCode.js](https://davidshimjs.github.io/qrcodejs/) for generating table QR codes
- Hosted on [GitHub Pages](https://pages.github.com/)

## Local development

Just open `index.html` in a browser — no build step needed. To test Firestore writes locally, make sure the `firebaseConfig` in the `<script>` tag points to the live project (it already does).

## Deployment

Pushing to `main` and enabling GitHub Pages (Settings → Pages → Deploy from branch → main → /root) is all that's needed — GitHub serves `index.html` automatically.

## Admin access

The guest-list/table-assignment panel is hidden behind a passcode (`MN2026`) — tap the small monogram icon in the footer 5 times within a few seconds to trigger it.